  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hydrogen bonding is responsible for the stacking of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>helix structure of protein.</p><p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>-helix structure of proteins is stabilized&nbsp;by intramolecular H-bonding between C&minus;O of one amino acid residue and the N&minus;H of the fourth amino acid residue in the chain.&nbsp;</p>",
